    :inserted-texts
    [" C15 record/stream refinement (Open; existing compiler/c15/structured-diagnostic): Validate actual produced records and streams against the canonical C15 schema, including artifact/diagnostic/rule/message-key, severity/lifecycle, primary and related location roles, origins, phase-available profile/target/syntax identity, typed facts, remediation and redactions. Support error, warning, info, hint and internal-error severity under their C15 emission rules; error prevents compilation/artifact emission and an internal-error retains compiler-invariant bug-report context. Preserve active, suppressed-by-policy, redacted, resolved-by-fix and stale-after-edit lifecycle states. Preserve the source/generated/macro/manifest/package/MIR/domain/backend/runtime location variants, selecting the most actionable source span as primary and downstream/generated context as related. Typed fact fields carry the applicable type/effect/capability/profile/ownership/safety/proof/target/provider/artifact facts, not prose substitutes. Stream records bind stage, input artifact, output artifact if any, diagnostics, actual summary counts by severity, deterministic ordering key, redaction policy and rendering version; attach them to pipeline and target manifests. Summary counts describe actual stream contents and impose no work allowance. Required outputs: schema/catalog/stream and manifest links, related-span/remediation/redaction records and positive/negative producer fixtures. Refuse malformed or missing required fields, invalid phase availability, lost location/origin/fact/remediation data, inconsistent severity summaries or ordering and missing stream-manifest links with the applicable C15-SCHEMA/SPAN/ORIGIN/FACTS/REMEDIATION/ORDER rules. Diagnostics about diagnostics retain producing stage, offending diagnostic identity, schema field, artifact and remediation. Consume actual stage/source/origin/fact products; a supplied schema or success flag cannot prove producer execution. Foundation diagnostic criterion gravity/foundation-diagnostic-context (Open): For an actual rejected D0-D4 or D7 contract, preserve the stable owning rule, failed thesis/layer/profile boundary and downstream document that owns the detailed rule. Include applicable source span or manifest entry, active profile/target, type/effect facts, missing effect/capability, unsafe audit identity when relevant, producing/consuming pass and remediation without inventing phase-unavailable values. Doc tooling, compiler manifest checks and governance consumers use the same diagnostic/artifact model; roadmap policy diagnostics block the unsupported release claim and type/effect errors retain stable IDs. Preserve D1-ARTIFACT-GAP for reported missing provenance edges, D4-INTEROP-UNTRACKED for a reported external-boundary record gap, and D7-MACRO-PROVENANCE and D7-PASS-CONTRACT for the reported origin/IR-fact failures. Required outputs: owning-checker rejection plus its structured contextual diagnostic and source/compiler/profile/target/manifest links. Exercise correctly attributed positive records and reject missing/stale rule, lost required context, raw host prose or substituted producer/pass identity. This record producer consumes the actual owning checker's failure and does not implement its legality rule, architecture decision, release admission or other foundation scope."
     " Criterion compiler/c15/diagnostic-views (Open): Derive CLI/text, JSON, IDE ranges, CI annotations, localized messages, known-ID explain pages and remediation/quick-fix views from the same validated, resolved C15 records. Preserve diagnostic identity, rule, severity, primary and related span roles, stage/profile/target, typed fact keys/values, remediation category/target, redaction markers and ordering across consumers. Required outputs: actual consumer rendering/quick-fix/explain artifacts, shared-record parity results and golden JSON fixtures. Positive fixtures compare the views and preserve identity/semantic golden results when human wording or localization improves. Reject view-only rule changes, lost origins/remediation, a golden mismatch, plain strings substituted for structured input and goldens keyed only to localized prose; retain C15-GOLDEN and applicable schema/identity/span/origin diagnostics. Consume actual diagnostic producer and identity/order outputs; view presence alone does not establish their implementation. Criterion compiler/c15/diagnostic-redaction (Open): Apply declared publication policy to secret values, private package internals, proprietary macro expansions and sensitive target details. Public views exclude secret values and raw model/tool outputs classified private while retaining enough structure to fix the issue and explicit redaction markers. Full records are kept only in authorized private artifact stores; suppression preserves the internal audit artifact. Package privacy may redact generated producer internals but must retain authorized origin evidence. A private construction record or unresolved digest request is not a resolved diagnostic or safe public projection. Required outputs: redaction/publication decision and report, authorized private/audit record, public view and accepted/refused boundary fixtures. Positive fixtures show useful redacted public output, authorized private access and retained suppressed audit data. Reject secret/private leakage, missing markers or useful context, unauthorized full-record access, lost audit/origin records and premature publication with C15-REDACTION and applicable identity/origin/schema diagnostics. Consume actual source/record/origin and publication-policy facts; no renderer or supplied authorization flag grants private-store authority."]}
